                <pb facs="0481" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/11–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-30T20:00:00-05:00">November 30,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>663. Bullard’s suggestions concerning possible advisability of provincial
                    elections throughout Iran have come to Dept’s attention. Your views would be
                    appreciated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
